  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Chef's friend Igzi is often at the coding gym, working out his mind muscles. When he is there, he asks Chef to guard his most prized posession: a sequence A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​. Initially, for each iii (1≤i≤N1 \\le i \\le N1≤i≤N), Ai=iA_i = iAi​=i held. However, Chef sometimes gets bored and starts playing with the sequence. Since NNN can be very large, Chef has a lot of fun with it and he would like to share it with you.\n\nYou should process QQQ queries of two types:\n\n\n`1 x`: set Ax=0A_x = 0Ax​=0\n`2 l r`: find the maximum element in the subsequence Al,Al+1,…,ArA_l, A_{l+1}, \\ldots, A_rAl​,Al+1​,…,Ar​\nSince Chef does not want to make Igzi angry, the queries are encoded so that they have to be processed online:\n\n\nFor each query, let's denote the sum of answers to all previous queries of type 2, modulo NNN, by sss. (Initially, s=0s = 0s=0.)\nFor each query of the first type, you are given an integer yyy. You can compute xxx as y+sy + sy+s.\nFor each query of the second type, you are given two integers ppp and qqq. You can compute lll as p+sp + sp+s and rrr as q+sq + sq+s.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤101 \\le T \\le 101≤T≤10",
      "1≤N≤10181 \\le N \\le 10^{18}1≤N≤1018",
      "1≤Q≤500,0001 \\le Q \\le 500,0001≤Q≤500,000",
      "1≤l≤r≤N1 \\le l \\le r \\le N1≤l≤r≤N",
      "1≤x≤N1 \\le x \\le N1≤x≤N",
      "the sum of QQQ over all test cases does not exceed 1,000,0001,000,0001,000,000",
      "Subtasks**Subtask #1 (10 points):** N,Q≤1,000N, Q \\le 1,000N,Q≤1,000",
      "**Subtask #2 (10 points):** N≤100,000N \\le 100,000N≤100,000",
      "**Subtask #3 (30 points):** each query of the second type appears after all queries of the first type"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "The first line of the input contains a single integer TTT denoting the number of test cases. The description of TTT test cases follows.\nThe first line of each test case contains two space-separated integers NNN and QQQ.\nThe following QQQ lines describe queries.\n\nEach of these lines starts with an integer ttt denoting the type of the current query: t=1t = 1t=1 for a query of the first type or t=2t = 2t=2 for a query of the second type.\nFor a query of the first type, it is followed by a space and an integer yyy.\nFor a query of the second type, it is followed by a space and two space-separated integers ppp and qqq.",
    "outputFormat": "For each query of the second type, print a single line containing one integer ― the maximum of the given subsequence.",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "1\n7 9\n2 2 5\n1 0\n2 -3 0\n1 1\n2 0 3\n1 -4\n1 -2\n2 -4 -1\n2 -5 -3",
        "output": "5  \n4\n4\n0\n1",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nQuery 1: l=2l = 2l=2, r=5r = 5r=5. The maximum element of the subsequence A2,A3,A4,A5A_2, A_3, A_4, A_5A2​,A3​,A4​,A5​ is A5=5A_5 = 5A5​=5. After this query, sss becomes 5%7=55\\%7 = 55%7=5.\nQuery 2: x=5x = 5x=5. A5A_5A5​ becomes 000.\nQuery 3: l=2l = 2l=2, r=5r = 5r=5. The maximum element of the same subsequence is now A4=4A_4 = 4A4​=4; sss becomes (5+4)%7=2(5+4)\\%7 = 2(5+4)%7=2.\nQuery 4: x=3x = 3x=3, A3A_3A3​ becomes 000.\nQuery 5: l=2l = 2l=2, r=5r = 5r=5. The maximum element of the same subsequence is still A4=4A_4 = 4A4​=4; sss becomes (5+4+4)%7=6(5+4+4)\\%7 = 6(5+4+4)%7=6.\nQuery 6: x=2x = 2x=2, A2A_2A2​ becomes 000.\nQuery 7: x=4x = 4x=4, A4A_4A4​ becomes 000.\nQuery 8: l=2l = 2l=2, r=5r = 5r=5. All elements of the same subsequence as before are 000, so the maximum is 000; sss becomes (5+4+4+0)%7=6(5+4+4+0)\\%7 = 6(5+4+4+0)%7=6.\nQuery 9: l=1l = 1l=1, r=3r = 3r=3. The maximum of the subsequence A1,A2,A3A_1, A_2, A_3A1​,A2​,A3​ is A1=1A_1 = 1A1​=1; sss becomes (5+4+4+0+1)%7=0(5+4+4+0+1)\\%7 = 0(5+4+4+0+1)%7=0."
      }
    ]
